#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/sr.rc -- Serbian (Cyrillic), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "sr"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. An adaptation, not a letter-for-letter translation (owner's word
// 198.14); the glossary of the language is l10n/glossary/sr.tsv in the control contour.
// The dictionary is the same as in sr-Latn.rc, which is this text letter for letter in Latin.
// Keys stay in Latin letters as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4);
// The quotation marks are „ “ and the full stop and the commas are the Latin ones (RULES 3).
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Serbian (Cyrillic) -- `[general] language = "sr"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
